  "263": {
    "inputs": {
      "text": "For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action cinematic film shot on 35mm motion picture film, organic and soft, not a digital render: muted cool gray-green tones with a subtle teal undertone, ARRI Alexa film grain and contrast, cinematic dramatic tone, gentle highlight roll-off, no digital sharpening, warm candlelight on his face and hands, the ruined stone hall in cool teal shadow. The scene continues exactly as in <Picture 1>: the bard sits frontally behind the old piano in the ruined castle hall, his hands on the worn ivory keys, candles burning at the sides of the frame. The piano is a massive, heavy antique instrument made of thick dark wood, fixed solidly to the stone floor, and it stays perfectly still for the whole video: the piano, its keyboard, the table surface and the candles never move, shake, bounce or vibrate, whatever the hands do. The piano, the candles and the hall stay exactly as in <Picture 1> throughout the whole video, unchanged. The camera is a very slow, smooth push-in with small amplitude toward his face, held frontal, with no shake. Only his fingers, hands, wrists and torso move. He plays like a real pianist and never stops until the last frame: his right hand plays a flowing melody in the upper register, the fingers pressing the keys lightly one after another, the thumb passing under the palm and the hand traveling to the right along the keyboard, while his left hand plays slow rolling arpeggios in the lower register and travels to the left, each finger rising and falling in turn. The keys sink only a few millimeters under each finger, his wrists are relaxed and floating, his hands glide along the keys in different positions, and no key is pounded. His torso sways gently with the phrasing and the candle flames flicker softly. The man in his late twenties with a rough, strong voice (S1) sings straight into the lens, lips, jaw and breathing precisely lip-synced to the provided audio: <d>[English] Who wants to wear the heavy crown?</d> His expression is grave, tense and bitter the whole time, his lips part only to sing, and he never smiles at any moment. His acting builds in order: before the first word he draws a short sharp breath and his chin lifts; on \"wear the heavy\" his brows draw together and his gaze hardens on the lens; on \"crown\" the melody climbs and both hands spread wider across the keyboard, his head pushing slightly forward; after the last word his fingers keep moving over the keys more slowly, his face grave and serious, his jaw set, his eyes heavy and fixed on the lens. His mouth stays fully visible, no large head turns.\n\noverall_soundscape: N/A\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A"
    },
    "class_type": "Text",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "𝙆 Text",
      "aux_id": "TFL-TFL/ComfyUI_Text_Translation",
      "ver": "495f9773dd3651a366ebac664fc4b0f301e9b1b3"
    }
